# NOBORU PERFORMANCE WORKFLOW

When doing performance work, follow this workflow.

## Authority

- Targets: `performance.mdc` (2s load, 300ms routes, 100ms actions, Lighthouse 90)
- Baseline audit: `docs/performance-audit.md`
- Prompt library: `docs/Performance Prompts/`
- Architecture: `architecture.mdc` — UI → Service → Repository → Database

## Before changing code

1. Read the relevant prompt in `docs/Performance Prompts/`
2. Check `docs/performance-audit.md` for priority (P1 first)
3. Profile or measure the hot path if the finding is unverified
4. State exit criteria (ms saved, calls reduced, Lighthouse delta)

## Execution order

Audit → DB queries → API batching → write queue/XP debounce → caching → virtualization → preloading → leaderboard/rate limits → assets

## Constraints

- No direct Supabase calls from UI
- Cache invalidation on progress mutations
- Offline buffers must flush safely on reconnect
- Use Vercel KV / Upstash for distributed cache and rate limits (not self-hosted Redis unless deployed)
- Batch endpoints exempt from tight per-action rate limits

## Existing systems to extend (not replace)

- `lib/cache/content-cache.ts` — curriculum cross-request cache
- `lib/cache/dashboard-cache.ts` — request-scoped dashboard dedupe
- `components/ui/windowed-list.tsx` — list virtualization
- `app/api/review/submit/batch/route.ts` — review batch pattern
- `features/offline/services/sync-server.service.ts` — offline batch sync

## After implementation

- Update `docs/performance-audit.md` if priority items are resolved
- Add or extend Lighthouse coverage for affected routes
- Verify no regression on offline learning paths

